# Dynamic Image Carousel Component

Use this pattern when building image carousels that resize the frame to match each image's aspect ratio (no white borders).

## HTML Structure

```html
<div class="carousel-wrap" data-carousel data-carousel-dynamic>
    <div class="carousel-track">
        <img src="..." alt="...">
        <img src="..." alt="...">
        <!-- more images -->
    </div>
    <div class="carousel-dots"></div>
</div>
```

**Required attributes:**
- `data-carousel` — enables carousel behavior
- `data-carousel-dynamic` — enables dynamic height (frame resizes per image)

## CSS (scope with parent class, e.g. `.bbo-page`)

```css
.carousel-wrap {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: height 0.4s ease;
}
.carousel-wrap[data-carousel-dynamic] {
    min-height: 200px;
}
.carousel-track {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1);
    will-change: transform;
}
.carousel-track img {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    object-fit: contain;
}
.carousel-dots {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
}
.carousel-dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(11,70,140,0.15);
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease;
}
.carousel-dot.active {
    background: var(--blue);
    transform: scale(1.3);
}
```

## JavaScript (vanilla, IIFE)

- Auto-advances every 3s
- Swipe support (touch)
- Dot navigation
- Dynamic height: `wrap.style.height = wrapWidth * (naturalHeight/naturalWidth)`
- Use `getBoundingClientRect().width` for accurate measurement
- Use double `requestAnimationFrame` when switching slides for layout
- Wrap in `DOMContentLoaded` for embed contexts (WordPress, etc.)

## Optional Enhanced Features (Not Default)

Carousels **may** support enhanced features (category tabs, photo albums, shuffle-no-repeat), but these must **not** be default. Only enable when explicitly opted in.

**Opt-in:** Use `data-carousel-features="categories,albums,shuffle"` (or a subset) on the carousel wrapper. Carousels without this attribute use basic behavior only.

**Features:**
- **Categories:** Clickable tabs to filter by category (e.g. General, Halloween, Beachlife)
- **Albums:** Per-category photo album view (grid + lightbox on click)
- **Shuffle:** Random order, no repeat until all images shown, then reshuffle

**Requirements when enabled:**
- Images need `data-category` (e.g. `general`, `halloween`, `beachlife`)
- **Lightbox:** All carousel and album images clickable → open lightbox with: left/right arrows to navigate catalogue, grey × top-right to close, click overlay or Escape to close
- Mobile: category tabs wrap; album grid uses `minmax(120px, 1fr)` at ≤480px, `minmax(140px, 1fr)` at 481–1024px, `minmax(160px, 1fr)` at ≥1025px
- Touch: swipe, tap-friendly category buttons, tap-to-open lightbox in carousel and albums

**Reference:** `Components/Index/carousel-pickleball-homepage.html`

## Single Source of Truth (Law)

**Never edit carousel image lists directly in HTML files.** Always edit the source of truth and run the universal build script.

**Workflow (required for every carousel):**
1. Edit the carousel's source markdown (e.g. `media/**/*-images.md`) — add, remove, or reorder URLs
2. Run: `node scripts/build/build-carousel.js scripts/build/carousel-configs/<name>.json`
3. The build injects images into all configured HTML targets

**Universal Build Script:** `scripts/build/build-carousel.js` — takes a JSON config file, no hardcoded values.

**Config files:** Stored in `scripts/build/carousel-configs/*.json`. Each config defines:
- `source` — markdown file with image URLs
- `targets` — HTML files to inject into
- `sections` — map section names → category/caption
- `altPatterns` — regex → alt text mappings
- `trackSelector` / `trackCloseIndent` — HTML injection points

**Categories module:** Source markdown uses `## Section Name` headers. The config's `sections` map matches these to `data-category` values and optional captions.

**Creating a new carousel (repeatable workflow):**

Use the scaffold script—output adheres to this mdc.

```bash
node scripts/scaffold/new-carousel.js <name> [--media-path=PATH] [--sections=a,b,c]
```

Example: `node scripts/scaffold/new-carousel.js tennis --sections=general,lessons,events`

Then:
1. Add image URLs to the generated markdown
2. Run `node scripts/build/build-carousel.js scripts/build/carousel-configs/<name>.json`
3. Scaffolded HTML links to Components/Carousel/template/carousel.css and carousel.js

**Manual alternative:** Create source markdown, config JSON+readme, and HTML with `data-carousel`/`data-carousel-dynamic`/`carousel-track`/`carousel-dots` per spec above.

